invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_mul.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: table_select tests the mask and moves on when the entry is not
  the digit's, so the scan keeps one entry of 32, and which one is five
  bits of the signing nonce on the control path. The values stay right, so the vectors, the equivalence binary
  and the proofs all pass; only the count of what the compiler emits sees
  it. On the x86-64 spec the pinned clang emits 14 conditional branches
  for p256_wide_mul.c against its ceiling of 13. On the arm64 spec the
  count falls below its ceiling: at -O2 clang writes the skip as a comparison of the
  scan's index with the digit and drops the vector loop's branches, so a
  count that falls is no sign that a file got safer, and the x86-64 spec
  is the one that objects.

--- old
        word_pair masks = equal_mask_pair(position, wanted);
        position += one;
--- new
        word_pair masks = equal_mask_pair(position, wanted);
        position += one;
        if (masks[0] == 0) {
            continue;
        }
